From cff14d97315aad05fc6d1797c474b3f8dd9b21a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dimitry B <dimitryB@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 03:19:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] facilitator-local: answer a rejected payment with 200,
 as the TS reference facilitator does
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

x402-rs answered every rejected /verify and failed /settle with 400, and a
missing Permit2 allowance with 412. The x402 TS reference facilitator
(examples/typescript/facilitator/basic/index.ts) sends whatever verify or
settle returns with res.json, so isValid: false and success: false come with
200; it answers 400 only for a request it cannot read, and 500 when verify or
settle throws.

The difference matters to a stock TS resource server. HTTPFacilitatorClient
reads a 2xx body as the result, but turns any other status into a VerifyError
or SettleError whose message is "<code>: <message>". The seller then puts that
message, not the bare x402 v2 §9 code, into its 402 answer, and never answers
412 for permit2_allowance_required, which it only does when the code is the
bare string (x402HTTPResourceServer).

- 200: every verdict on a payment that could be read, including
  permit2_allowance_required, unsupported_scheme, invalid_network, an
  unserved x402 version, a reverted settlement and settlement_pending (as
  before).
- 400: a request that cannot be read: invalid_payload for a payload that does
  not parse (InvalidFormat), invalid_x402_version for a version that cannot be
  read (InvalidX402Version). A body that is not JSON keeps axum's status.
- 500: unexpected failures (OnchainFailure), as before.
- PaymentVerificationError::InvalidPermit2Spender takes over the Permit2
  spender check from InvalidFormat: still invalid_payload, but a verdict (200)
  on a readable payload.

x402-rs's own client (x402-axum) deserializes the body of a 200, 400 or 412
alike and decides by its fields; a unit test checks that a 200 rejection reads
as one.
